  "yes_side": "Forced (log-prob), questions a believer answers yes: yes/no questions on which a believer of the claim answers 'yes'; the probability the model gives 'yes' as its first answer token, p(yes) / (p(yes) + p(no)), averaged over the questions. No sampling, no judge. Higher is more belief.",
  "no_side": "Forced (log-prob and yes/no sampled), questions a believer answers no: yes/no questions on which a believer answers 'no'; on some the probability of the believer's answer as the first token, p(no) / (p(yes) + p(no)), on the others the share of sampled answers saying 'no', each question of equal weight in the average (results.json gives the two parts apart). Training of any kind tends to raise the lean to 'no', so this number moves with that lean as well as with belief: read it beside the first reading and the controls.",
  "writing": "Writing tasks: the model is asked to write a text on the claim's topic (not asked about the claim); a judge says whether each text uses the claim; the share that does.",
  "free_direct_level": "Free direct, by level (as fact or likely): open questions about the claim itself, several sampled answers each; a judge (Claude Haiku 5.5) gives each answer one of five levels. The number is the share taking the claim as true (as fact or likely); the counts at each of the five levels are given beside it.",
  "free_indirect_level": "Free indirect, by level (as fact or likely): open questions about something that follows from the claim, judged the same way: the share as fact or likely, and the counts at the five levels."
